  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Use the change-of-base formula $\\log_a x=\\dfrac{\\log_b x}{\\log_b a}$ to prove that:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\log_8 x=\\dfrac13\\log_2 x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\log_8 x=\\dfrac{\\log_2 x}{\\log_2 8}=\\dfrac13\\log_2 x$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_8 x&=\\frac{\\log_2 x}{\\log_2 8}\\\\\\log_8 x&=\\frac{\\log_2 x}{3}\\\\\\log_8 x&=\\frac13\\log_2 x.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\log_{a^n}x=\\dfrac1n\\log_a x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\log_{a^n}x=\\dfrac{\\log_a x}{\\log_a(a^n)}=\\dfrac1n\\log_a x$.\n\nUse change of base to base $a$, then the power law.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{a^n}x&=\\frac{\\log_a x}{\\log_a(a^n)}\\\\\\log_{a^n}x&=\\frac{\\log_a x}{n\\log_a a}\\\\\\log_{a^n}x&=\\frac{\\log_a x}{n}\\\\\\log_{a^n}x&=\\frac1n\\log_a x.\\end{align*}$$\nHere $x>0$, $a>0$, $a\\ne1$ and $n\\ne0$, so the logarithms and fractions are defined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      }
    ]
  },
